Routing issues:
1. "Active route filters to active todos only" - clicking the route filter doesn't filter the todos. The app shows all 2 items instead of just 1.
2. "Completed route filters to completed todos only" - similar issue.
3. "Selected filter link has the 'selected' class" - clicking the filter link doesn't add the 'selected' class.
4. "Active filter is persisted on reload" - filter isn't persisted because the click didn't work.
5. "Checking a todo in a filtered view hides it" - times out, likely because the filter route isn't working.

The issue is that my app.js doesn't handle routing/filtering via hash changes. I need to add hash change listener and filtering logic.

Looking at the Given steps for routing, they use "When the user clicks the filter link" which triggers a click on the anchor element. In a real browser, clicking an anchor with href="#/active" would change the hash and trigger a hashchange event. But in happy-dom, the click event doesn't trigger navigation.

Let me check my When step:
```
When('the user clicks the {string} filter link', async function (filterName) {
  const filterMap = { 'All': '#/', 'Active': '#/active', 'Completed': '#/completed' };
  const hash = filterMap[filterName];
  if (hash) {
    const link = this.document.querySelector('a[href="' + hash + '"]');
    if (link) {
      this.click(link);
    }
  }
});
```

This clicks the link but doesn't trigger a hash change. Let me also update the URL hash when clicking filter links. And I need to add hashchange handling in app.js.

Let me update both:
1. In the When step, also update the hash after clicking the link
2. In app.js, add hashchange listener and routing logic

